{"sha":"6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","node_id":"C_kwDOO6Fx59oAKDZlN2Y3YjVjOGU0NTAyY2IzZTZmNmVlMjBkMzBiNzJlYmJlNjk3ZjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tsiorintsoa","email":"stsiorintsoa@ufl.edu","date":"2026-01-21T03:58:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"Tsiorintsoa","email":"stsiorintsoa@ufl.edu","date":"2026-01-21T03:58:37Z"},"message":"Added general README and a Dockerfile","tree":{"sha":"4a13829d2090894fa53b2d57be5777616423ba6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/git/trees/4a13829d2090894fa53b2d57be5777616423ba6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/git/commits/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/commits/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","html_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/commit/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/commits/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/comments","author":null,"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"6f5e6b576be1f3e08838840f773548255245aa47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/commits/6f5e6b576be1f3e08838840f773548255245aa47","html_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/commit/6f5e6b576be1f3e08838840f773548255245aa47"}],"stats":{"total":492,"additions":462,"deletions":30},"files":[{"sha":"d851f8414825b7dbc2392593cad06be12ec30aea","filename":"Dockerfile","status":"added","additions":47,"deletions":0,"changes":47,"blob_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/blob/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/Dockerfile","raw_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/raw/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/Dockerfile","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/contents/Dockerfile?ref=6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@\n+# Use a base image with CMake and GCC\n+FROM ubuntu:22.04\n+\n+ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\n+\n+# Install dependencies\n+RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n+        locales \\\n+        build-essential \\\n+        cmake \\\n+        openjdk-17-jdk \\\n+        python3 python3-pip && \\\n+    locale-gen en_US.UTF-8 && \\\n+    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n+\n+ENV LANG=en_US.UTF-8 \\\n+    LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 \\\n+    JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=\"-Dfile.encoding=UTF.8\"\n+\n+# Set working directory\n+WORKDIR /app\n+\n+# Copy the project files into the container\n+COPY . .\n+\n+# Make a build directory\n+RUN mkdir ./cpp/build\n+\n+# Configure and build the project\n+RUN cd ./cpp/build && cmake .. && make\n+\n+RUN cp ./cpp/build/PAIpp ./PAIpp\n+\n+# Create the bin/ directory\n+RUN mkdir -p ./java/bin\n+\n+# Find and copy all .java files from src/ to bin/\n+RUN find ./java/src -name \"*.java\" -exec javac -d java/bin {} +\n+\n+RUN jar cfe jPAI.jar edu.uf.main.Main -C java/bin .\n+\n+RUN chmod +x /app/run.sh\n+\n+ENV APP_MODE=cpp\n+\n+ENTRYPOINT [\"/app/run.sh\"]\n+"},{"sha":"035e6f26a46d92165da83e174c7b1b88a885d434","filename":"README.md","status":"added","additions":281,"deletions":0,"changes":281,"blob_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/blob/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/raw/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/contents/README.md?ref=6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,281 @@\n+# PAI\n+\n+java Pulmonary Agent-based Infection simulator\n+\n+This project is a C++ and Java cross-platform project. Buidable on Windows, Linux, and macOS via terminal and has a built docker image.\n+\n+## Using this project with Docker\n+\n+Without installing any dependencies, this project has a ready-to-run Docker image.\n+\n+- Docker version 29.1.3 (https://www.docker.com/)\n+\n+### Pull the Image \n+\n+```bash\n+docker pull ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage\n+```\n+### Run the Container\n+\n+**For C++**: \n+```bash\n+docker run --rm ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage cpp <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```bash\n+docker run --rm ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage cpp 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+\n+**For Java**: \n+```bash\n+docker run --rm ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage java <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```bash\n+docker run --rm ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage java 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+\n+**For C++ test**: \n+```bash\n+docker run --rm ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage ctest\n+```\n+\n+**For Java test**: \n+```bash\n+docker run --rm ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai/paiimage jtest\n+```\n+\n+## To create a local image\n+```bash\n+docker build -t <myimage> .\n+```\n+Example\n+```bash\n+docker build -t paiimage .\n+```\n+\n+Without a Docker, this project can be build and run separately.\n+\n+# PAIpp\n+\n+This is the C++ cross-platform project built with CMake. Buidable on Windows, Linux, and macOS via terminal.\n+\n+## Build Instructions\n+\n+See [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md) in **cpp/** directory for platform-specific instructions.\n+\n+### Quick Start (Unix/macOS/Linux)\n+\n+```bash\n+git clone https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI.git\n+cd PAI/cpp\n+cmake -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+./build/PAIpp <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+\n+### macOS\n+\n+#### Requirements\n+\n+- Xcode CLI Tools (for clang++ and make)\n+\n+```bash\n+xcode-select --install\n+brew install cmake\n+```\n+#### Build\n+\n+```bash\n+cmake -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+./build/PAIpp <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+\n+### Windows (MinGW)\n+\n+#### Requirements\n+\n+- MinGW\n+- Add mingw32-make to PATH\n+- CMake\n+\n+#### Build\n+\n+```bash\n+cmake -G \"MinGW Makefiles\" -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+./build/PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+\n+From Command prompt or PowerShell:\n+\n+```batch\n+cmake -G \"MinGW Makefiles\" -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```batch\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+### Windows (Cygwin)\n+\n+#### Requirements\n+\n+- Cygwin\n+- Add cygwin to PATH\n+- CMake\n+\n+#### Build\n+\n+```bash\n+cmake -G \"Unix Makefiles\" -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+./build/PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+From Command prompt or PowerShell:\n+\n+```batch\n+cmake -G \"Unix Makefiles\" -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```batch\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+\n+### Linux/Unix/\n+\n+#### Requirements\n+\n+- g++\n+- cmake\n+\n+```bash \n+sudo apt get update\n+sudo apt install g++\n+sudo apt install cmake\n+```\n+#### Build\n+\n+```bash\n+cmake -S . -B build\n+cmake --build build\n+./build/PAIpp <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+Example\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+## Clean build\n+\n+```bash\n+rm -rf build\n+```\n+\n+From Command prompt or PowerShell:\n+```batch\n+rmdir /s /q build\n+```\n+\n+## Test\n+\n+The script `test_paipp.py`:\n+\n+- Runs the `PAIpp` simulation with two different sets of inputs\n+- Captures its tabular output\n+- Checks key quantities at specific iterations (0, 180, 360, 720, 1440, and. 2045):\n+  - **Aspergillus** (column 2)\n+  - **TNF** (column 19)\n+  - **Macrophages** (column 22)\n+- Confirms these outputs are within expected ranges.\n+\n+### How to Run\n+\n+Make sure both `PAIpp` and `test_paipp.py` are in the same directory. Then run:\n+\n+```bash\n+python3 test_paipp.py\n+```\n+\n+test_paipp.py was tested with Python version 3.7.2.\n+\n+This test is designed to see if output values are within reasonable bounds. Because of the stochastic nature of the simulator, passing the test is probable but not guaranteed.\n+\n+\n+# jPAI\n+java Pulmonary Agent-based Infection simulator\n+\n+This is the java cross-platform project build with javac. Buidable on Windows, Linux, and macOS via terminal.\n+\n+- Java Runtime Environment (JRE) 8 or later  \n+  (Tested with Java 18.0.2)\n+\n+  If you have `jPAI.jar`:\n+\n+```bash\n+java -jar jPAI.jar <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+\n+Example\n+```bash\n+java -jar jPAI.jar 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+\n+## Build Instructions\n+\n+- java 1.8\n+- javac 1.8\n+\n+### Unix/macOS/Linux\n+\n+```bash\n+git clone https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI.git\n+cd PAI/java\n+javac -d bin $(find . -name \"*.java\")\n+jar cfe jPAI.jar edu.uf.main.Main -C bin .\n+```\n+\n+### Windows\n+\n+Command Prompt or PowerShell\n+\n+```batch\n+javac -d bin $(Get-ChildItem -Path . -Filter *.java -Recurse | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName })\n+jar cfe jPAI.jar edu.uf.main.Main -C bin .\n+```\n+\n+## Test\n+\n+The script `test_jpai.py`:\n+\n+- Runs the `jPAI.jar` simulation with two different sets of inputs\n+- Captures its tabular output\n+- Checks key quantities at specific iterations (0, 180, 360, 720, 1440, and. 2045):\n+  - **Aspergillus** (column 2)\n+  - **TNF** (column 19)\n+  - **Macrophages** (column 22)\n+- Confirms these outputs are within expected ranges.\n+\n+### How to Run\n+\n+Make sure both `jPAI.jar` and `test_jpai.py` are in the same directory. Then run:\n+\n+```bash\n+python3 test_jpai.py\n+```\n+\n+test_jpai.py was tested with Python version 3.7.2\n+\n+This test is designed to see if output values are within reasonable bounds. Because of the stochastic nature of the simulator, passing the test is probable but not guaranteed.\n+"},{"sha":"22f50ebdf2d82b082fdf17a4d5a48497b9c0068a","filename":"cpp/INSTALL.md","status":"modified","additions":53,"deletions":25,"changes":78,"blob_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/blob/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/cpp%2FINSTALL.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/raw/6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5/cpp%2FINSTALL.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/contents/cpp%2FINSTALL.md?ref=6e7f7b5c8e4502cb3e6f6ee20d30b72ebbe697f5","patch":"@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ This project uses CMake to configure and build on multiple platforms. Below are\n \n ### Prerequisites\n \n-- **MinGW**: Install MinGW to get a compatible GCC toolchain. You can download MinGW from [here](https://sourceforge.net/projects/mingw/).\n+- **MinGW**: Install MinGW to get a compatible GCC toolchain. You can download MinGW from [here](https://sourceforge.net/projects/mingw/). Mark **ming32-gcc-g++** and **mingw32-make** for installation and add **MinGW\\bin** to PATH.\n - **CMake**: Download and install CMake from [here](https://cmake.org/download/).\n \n ### Building the Project\n@@ -36,6 +36,25 @@ This project uses CMake to configure and build on multiple platforms. Below are\n     cmake -S -B build -G \"MinGW Makefiles\"\n     cmake --build build\n ```\n+### Running the Executable\n+Run the executable directly:\n+\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+\n+Example:\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n+```batch\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```\n+\n+Example:\n+```batch\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n ## Windows (Visual Studio)\n \n ### Prerequisites\n@@ -64,23 +83,30 @@ This project uses CMake to configure and build on multiple platforms. Below are\n     cmake -S -B build -G \"Visual Studio 16 2019\"\n     cmake --build build\n ```\n-\n ### Running the Executable\n+Run the executable directly:\n \n-```bash \n-./PAIpp <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n ```\n-From Command Prompt or PowerShell:\n \n+Example:\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n ```batch\n-.\\PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n ```\n \n+Example:\n+```batch\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n+```\n ## Windows (Cygwin)\n \n ### Prerequisites\n \n-- **Cygwin**: Install MinGW to get a compatible GCC toolchain. You can download MinGW from [here](https://sourceforge.net/projects/mingw/).\n+- **Cygwin**: Install MinGW to get a compatible GCC toolchain. You can download MinGW from [here](https://www.cygwin.com/).\n - **CMake**: Download and install CMake from [here](https://cmake.org/download/).\n \n ### Building the Project\n@@ -108,28 +134,35 @@ From Command Prompt or PowerShell:\n     cmake -S -B build -G \"Unix Makefiles\"\n     cmake --build build\n ```\n-\n ### Running the Executable\n+Run the executable directly:\n \n-```bash \n-./PAIpp <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n ```\n-From Command prompt or PowerShell:\n-\n Example:\n-```batch\n-./PAIpp 15 1920 15 640\n+```bash\n+./build/PAIpp.exe 15 1920 15 640\n ```\n-\n ```batch\n-.\\PAIpp.exe <num_neutrophils> <num_aspergillus> <num_macrophages> <num_pneumocytes>\n+.\\build\\PAIpp.exe <num